ce-matrix.md, TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz (validation-*.log, mutants.log), internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md in the candidate, the exclusion handoff TASK-260909-2ez769_exclusion-handoff.md (row 21), the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md Sections 13.14.1, 7.8 and 10.2.\\n\\nVerify with your own instruments: (1) Spec fidelity — extract the closed shapes yourself from the pinned text (Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 members and entry fields; Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 members, Source Basis union ax_session|external_native, Capture Boundary stable|unstable_archive with its proof coupling, Capture Item class vocabulary durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|credential|machine_auth|runtime_state|transient_lock|unknown with the included/excluded rule, exact excluded classes, core-derived raw_complete, creator/time, extensions; Canonical Session and Canonical Event with the 26-kind vocabulary, visibility, kind-selected payload, SourceEvidence, ordinal contiguity; identities and immutable generations) and diff member-by-member against rawmanifest.go/capturebuild.go/captureitem.go/boundary.go/session.go/event.go/identity.go/generation.go/blobref.go; a member the code admits that the text forbids, or a vocabulary entry missing, is a finding. (2) Refusal census — enumerate every refusal arm of the constructors and validators; each needs a named test reaching it through the production entry; then plant your own: an unknown class that does not set raw_complete=false, an included item carrying a reason, an excluded item carrying content, a credential/machine_auth/runtime_state/transient_lock class marked included, unsorted or duplicate entries, a total_bytes that disagrees with the entry sum, a Capture Boundary stable without its proof, unstable_archive without generation/pre-post digests, a Canonical Session with two main actors or an event ID not in the head subset, an event with a payload for the wrong kind, non-contiguous ordinals, a native key with an absolute path, embedded credential, AX marker or control character, a generation token compared by prefix — each must be refused with the exact class. (3) Exclusion (row 21) — the member allowlist must reject hosttrust.MatchExcludedFromReplication and ExcludedConfigDirName matches at construction: drive every excluded class from the handoff (host-channel/trust.json, pending-commit.json, credentials/, lock, .trust-stage-*, .custody-stage-*, lock-stage-*) plus an absolute path and a `..` escape; confirm a constructor negative exists per class and that nothing admits them through a different entry point (census the package for construction paths). (4) The provhost attestation bound — the leaf changed blobref.go to CalculateObjectIdentity with a local claim comparison after TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding reddened: confirm the census is green on this tree, that no non-test call to VerifyObjectIdentity exists outside internal/sessrepo (grep the module), and that the wrong-claim negative plus the N-descriptor-claim mutant actually pin the new gate (plant a comparison that accepts any claim and confirm the kill). (5) Blob install — Section 10.2 identity/byte-count agreement through localstore.PutBlob: positives plus a descriptor whose byte count or digest disagrees, and a no-replace attempt with different bytes; if the install is durable, exercise a crash between write and receipt (or confirm the landed localstore discipline covers it and state the bound). (6) Mutation — rerun testdata/mutant_harness.py in an isolated copy (17 KILLED + control), rerun each KILLED twice, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on arms the producer did not mutate (raw_complete derivation ignoring one unknown item; the excluded-class set missing one class; sorted-unique accepting an equal-key duplicate; the native-key sanitizer allowing one control character) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (7) The red race gate — the producer reports internal/sessquery exceeding the default 10m race timeout on this host (passes with -timeout 25m in 630s) and explicitly does NOT claim it as a pass. Judge it: is the package untouched by this change (import census), is the timeout a host-capacity artifact (compare with the 96s figure recorded in the STORY-260830-1oqfec landing checks when the machine was idle), and is the honest disclosure the right disposition, or must the leaf make the gate green (e.g. by not running four suites concurrently — an orchestration matter, not a candidate defect)? Rerun it yourself while nothing else runs and record your measurement. (8) Bounds and hygiene — the sibling bounds (per-kind payload fact registries, maximal_safe planning, G2 admission, Section 7.8 operation wiring, traceability bindings for the final leaf) are stated, not silently skipped; README package section with test commands and no capability claim; internal/traceability untouched; changed_paths exactly the candidate paths, no __pycache__/.pyc; gofmt/vet clean; go test ./internal/clonebundle ./internal/provhost ./internal/localstore ./internal/canonicaljson -count=1 green; tracecheck and `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit 0 on the exact tree.\\n\\nMethod: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-24z2b3/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-verdict-rev2.md and TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-24z2b3, revision=2, evidence=TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-verdict-rev2.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: claude-opus-5 max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7164,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1791,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
