{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5a7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0cc-369a-7993-946b-ef774181fd54"},"sequence":302,"recorded_at":1780531400000599,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0ccd9af720e8cf0074169dfd8a6","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-24z2b3/TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-24z2b3 — Review verdict, Change Request revision 2\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260917-c05bc8 (claude-opus-5, reviewer/reviewer).\n4|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-24z2b3-2` revision 2, base\n5|`888ae3dff6a55c29bfaf311957748d405ed1ab06`, candidate tree\n6|`bee4c80724cee011a1bdde7a59b0479637046769` (21 paths; patch sha256\n7|`c11360377daab6b6b2cfa34c1570cf452e1df9b411f55e55586505e8b7608f67`).\n8|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md` §13.14.1, §7.8, §10.2 and the\n9|common logical data model (§1.6, lines 286–337).\n10|\n11|## Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED → `to-dev`\n12|\n13|Two P1 correctness holes in gates the leaf claims to own, four P2 fidelity /\n14|evidence gaps, and P3 hygiene. The member-level spec fidelity, the row-21\n15|exclusion gate, the provhost bound, the blob install path and the race gate\n16|are all clean — the rework is narrow (see \"Rework scope\"). Nothing here is a\n17|Stop-The-Line.\n18|\n19|Method: isolated immutable copy of the exact candidate tree\n20|(`git archive bee4c807…` → `.temp/TASK-260830-24z2b3/candidate`, `.task-board`\n21|artifact dropped); the live Story worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never\n22|touched (`git status` unchanged: ` M LOGBOOK.md`, ` M README.md`,\n23|`?? internal/clonebundle/`; the temp-index tree of the live worktree equals\n24|`bee4c807…`). Every plant and probe below ran through the production entry\n25|points; raw logs are in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz`\n26|(`logs/`, `logs/mutants/*.log` one raw `go test` log per plant per run with\n27|the subprocess exit code, `reviewer_mutants.py`, `refusal_census.py`,\n28|`zz_review_probe_test.go.txt`, `zz_review_probe2_test.go.txt`).\n29|\n30|## Findings\n31|\n32|### P1-a — Descriptor identity is never linked to the entry (`rawmanifest.go`, `blobref.go`)\n33|\n34|`VerifyDescriptorAgreement(descriptor, wantBlobID, wantSize)` checks the\n35|descriptor's own claim against its omit-self digest and its `blob_id`/`size`\n36|against the entry, but nothing ever compares the entry's\n37|`blob_descriptor_id` with the identity of the descriptor bytes that were\n38|verified. Consequences, all witnessed through production entries\n39|(`logs/probes-01.log`):\n40|\n41|- `BuildRawObjectManifest` with `inputs[0].DescriptorID =\n42|  sha256(\"some-other-descriptor\")` and the real descriptor bytes: **ADMITTED**\n43|  — a sealed manifest whose entry references a descriptor that does not\n44|  exist (probe P1).\n45|- `DecodeRawObjectManifest` of that manifest: ADMITTED (P1b — expected,\n46|  structure only).\n47|- `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` with a fetch that returns the real\n48|  descriptor bytes for the wrong ID: **ADMITTED** (P1c) — the \"evidence\"\n49|  entry accepts any descriptor whose blob ID and size agree, regardless of\n50|  whether it is the descriptor the entry names.\n51|- Mutant `R-descriptor-id-unlinked2` (after agreement passes, the sealed\n52|  `blob_descriptor_id` is replaced by `sha256(input.DescriptorID)`, an\n53|  unrelated digest): **SURVIVED** the whole suite 3/3.\n54|\n55|§13.14.1: \"Each entry has … blob ID, Blob Descriptor ID … The descriptor\n56|agrees with blob ID and byte count\" — the descriptor that must agree is the\n57|one the entry identifies. Fix: `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` (or the two\n58|callers) must also require `calculated == entry.BlobDescriptorID`; add the\n59|negative (`DescriptorID` ≠ descriptor identity) at build, at\n60|`VerifyRawManifestDescriptors`, and a narrowing mutant for the new arm.\n61|\n62|### P1-b — The forked omit-self identity path lacks the AX number model (`decode.go` `omitSelfDigest`/`canonicalizeObject`)\n63|\n64|Extension values are the only member class whose numbers are not\n65|uint53-validated by the shape decoders, and they flow into the identity\n66|through the package's own `omitSelfDigest`, which uses lenient\n67|`encoding/json` decoding plus `canonicaljson.Canonicalize` — the exact fork\n68|the owner warns about (\"a caller that needs the AX number model must reach\n69|it through one of the entry points named above rather than by canonicalizing\n70|first\", `canonical.go:214-221`). Witnessed (`logs/probes-01.log`):\n71|\n72|- `BuildRawObjectManifest(... extensions={\"com.example.f\":1.5,\n73|  \"com.example.big\": 1<<60})`: **ADMITTED**; the sealed bytes carry\n74|  `\"com.example.big\":1152921504606847000` — 2^60 = 1152921504606846976 was\n75|  **rounded and the build continued** (P2c/P2e), and `DecodeRawObjectManifest`\n76|  admits the result (P2d).\n77|- `omitSelfDigest` over `1.5`, `9007199254740993`, `1e2`, `-0`: ADMITTED\n78|  (P2); only `1E400` fails, and only because `strconv.ParseFloat` overflows.\n79|\n80|Common logical data model (SPEC.v0.6.0.md:305-310): \"forbids floating-point\n81|values … A decoder MUST reject a numeric literal at or beyond 2^53 …\n82|Implementations MUST NOT round a value and continue.\" The same fork also\n83|collapses nested duplicate members inside extension values (lenient decode;\n84|`canonicaljson.decodeValue` refuses them at every depth): a manifest carrying\n85|`\"extensions\":{\"com.example.x\":{\"a\":1,\"a\":2}}`, resealed over the collapsed\n86|form, is **ADMITTED** by `DecodeRawObjectManifest` (probes D1/D2,\n87|`logs/probes-03-nested-duplicate.log`). Fix: validate extension values recursively at Build and\n88|Decode (integer literals only, |n| ≤ 2^53−1, no fraction/exponent, nested\n89|objects duplicate-free), or route the omit-self through an owner entry that\n90|carries the guarantee; add negatives and a narrowing mutant (admit exactly\n91|`2^53`).\n92|\n93|### P2-a — String bounds measured in bytes, forking the environ measure and contradicting the spec (`decode.go:111-127`, every `len(...)` bound in the Build paths)\n94|\n95|SPEC.v0.6.0.md:337: \"`string[n..m]` bounds UTF-8 characters\".\n96|`environ.StringLength` counts runes (\"Section 1.6 string measure in\n97|characters, not bytes\"; sessadapter and dirnode delegate to it so \"the two can\n98|never drift\"). `clonebundle.stringLength` returns `len(value)` and its\n99|comment asserts the opposite convention. Witness (`logs/probes-02-string-measure.log`):\n100|a 300-character / 600-byte native key is refused by `BuildRawObjectManifest`\n101|(\"not a string[1..512]\") and a 3000-character title by both\n102|`BuildCanonicalSession` and `DecodeCanonicalSession`, while\n103|`environ.CheckStringBounds(300 chars, 1..512)` admits. Over-strict only (bytes\n104|≥ characters), so no admit hole, but a conformant peer's manifest is refused\n105|here and the leaf forks the one repository measure. Fix: delegate to\n106|`environ.CheckStringBounds`/`StringLength` (and rune-count the Build-side\n107|`len()` checks), fix the comment, add one multibyte boundary row.\n108|\n109|### P2-b — Decode-side gates are unmeasured: 10 narrowing plants (plus one informational) survive the whole suite (3/3 each)\n110|\n111|The refusal census (`logs/refusal-census.log`, coverage-driven over every\n112|`invalid(` site) counts 359 refusal sites, 156 covered, 203 uncovered. Most\n113|rules are pinned once on the Build side and duplicated as separate code on\n114|the Decode side, where no named test reaches them. Plants against the exact\n115|candidate tree, `-run Test` (whole suite), deterministic over three runs\n116|(`logs/mutants-reviewer-run1.log`, `logs/mutants-repeats-run2-3.log`):\n117|\n118|| Plant | Site | Weakening | Verdict |\n119||---|---|---|---|\n120|| R-capture-items-dup-decode | `capturebuild.go:345` | `<=`→`<` (equal-key duplicate item) | SURVIVED 3/3 |\n121|| R-sorted-digests-dup-decode | `decode.go:259` | `<=`→`<` (duplicate digest; heads/parents/fingerprints) | SURVIVED 3/3 |\n122|| R-sorted-strings-dup-decode | `decode.go:233` | `<=`→`<` (duplicate string; excluded_classes/reason_codes) | SURVIVED 3/3 |\n123|| R-rawrefs-dup-decode | `event.go:196` | `<= 0`→`< 0` (duplicate raw_ref) | SURVIVED 3/3 |\n124|| R-decode-item-class | `captureitem.go:109` | admit exactly class `mystery` | SURVIVED 3/3 |\n125|| R-decode-actor-main-parent | `session.go:71` | admit exactly actor[0] main-with-parent | SURVIVED 3/3 |\n126|| R-decode-evidence-status | `event.go:279` | admit exactly `capture_status=maybe` | SURVIVED 3/3 |\n127|| R-decode-event-visibility | `event.go:547` | admit exactly `visibility=secret` | SURVIVED 3/3 |\n128|| R-verify-descriptors-skip-0 | `rawmanifest.go:419` | skip disagreement at entry 0 | SURVIVED 3/3 |\n129|| R-install-site-claim | `blobref.go:72` | install-site claim comparison disabled | SURVIVED 3/3 |\n130|| R-sanitizer-admits-0x01 | `identity.go:292` | admit exactly U+0001 | SURVIVED 3/3 (informational; the class is pinned at \\x00, \\x1f, \\x7f — R-sanitizer-admits-0x1f KILLED) |\n131|\n132|Every one of these arms does refuse when reached (probes P10–P12 all\n133|REFUSED), so the code is right and the evidence is missing. The DoD row\n134|\"every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant\" is not met for the Decode\n135|entries the conformance matrix names as call sites (rows 6, 7, 12, 13, 16,\n136|17, 18). Decode-side rules that ARE pinned (my plants KILLED 2/2): raw entry\n137|class and total_bytes and order at decode, session head-subset at decode,\n138|capture-manifest `raw_complete`+unknown at decode, both exclusion arms by\n139|true narrowing (`logs/mutants-extra.log`).\n140|\n141|### P2-c — Positive-only evidence on two verifying entries; one mutant row over-claims\n142|\n143|- `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` has no negative test (matrix row 18 cites\n144|  only `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`); its three refusal arms\n145|  (`rawmanifest.go:414/417/420`) are uncovered and `R-verify-descriptors-skip-0`\n146|  survives. Probes P15/P15b/P15c show the arms work.\n147|- `InstallRawBlob`'s own claim comparison (`blobref.go:72`) and its\n148|  `blob_id`/`size` arms (77/81) are uncovered; `R-install-site-claim`\n149|  (`&& false` at the install site only) survives. The shipped\n150|  `N-descriptor-claim` row patches both sites (`count=2`) and its note says\n151|  \"at both agreement and install sites\", but the kill comes only from the\n152|  `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` site (`TestBlobAgreementRefusals` resealed\n153|  descriptor). One measured site is being reported as two.\n154|\n155|### P2-d — `deriveRawComplete` admits duplicate raw keys hiding a missing included object (`capturebuild.go:420-427`)\n156|\n157|`deriveRawComplete(items{a,b included}, planKeys=[a,b], rawKeys=[a,a])`\n158|returns **true** (probe P4; `false` wanted): the \"all and only included\n159|objects\" check compares `len(included)` with `len(rawKeys)` and then only\n160|tests membership of each raw key, so a duplicate defeats the \"all\" half.\n161|`planKeys` duplicates are refused (P4b), so the two halves are asymmetric.\n162|`VerifyCaptureReconciliation` is a public verification entry taking\n163|`[]string`; it must refuse duplicate raw keys (or take the decoded\n164|`RawObjectManifest`). Add the negative and a narrowing mutant.\n165|\n166|### P2-e — `IdentityDigest`/`EncodeNativeIdentity` seal identities that `DecodeNativeIdentity` refuses (`identity.go:127`, `rawmanifest.go:428`)\n167|\n168|`IdentityDigest(NativeIdentity{IdentityKind:\"bogus\",…}, nil)` and\n169|`IdentityDigest(valid, {\"no-dots\":1})` both return a digest (probes P9/P9b).\n170|The doc comment claims \"encoding never admits what decoding refused\"; the\n171|matrix (rows 4 and 15) names `IdentityDigest` as the `source_identity_digest`\n172|production entry, and §13.14.1 defines that member as the digest of\n173|*canonical sanitized* `NativeIdentity` bytes. `buildCaptureManifest` already\n174|re-decodes the encoded bytes; `IdentityDigest` must do the same before\n175|hashing. Add the negatives (bad kind, bad extension key, unsanitized opaque\n176|identity) and a narrowing mutant.\n177|\n178|### P2-f — `decode.go` re-implements the landed environ gate set instead of adopting it (architecture)\n179|\n180|`rawUint53`, `checkDigest`, `checkUUIDv7`, `checkTimestamp`,\n181|`checkSortedUniqueStrings`, `checkSortedUniqueDigests`, `checkStringBounds`\n182|duplicate `environ.CheckUint53Bounds`, `CheckDigest`, `CheckUUIDv7`,\n183|`CheckTimestamp`, `CheckSortedUniqueStrings`, `CheckSortedUniqueDigests`,\n184|`CheckStringBounds`, which sessadapter and dirnode already delegate to. The\n185|COMMON CONTRACT says \"never fork a second model; extend or adopt\". The fork\n186|is where P2-a lives and where the unmeasured uniqueness arms of P2-b live.\n187|Delegate; keep only the package-specific rules (sanitizer, exclusion,\n188|coupling, reconciliation).\n189|\n190|### P3 — hygiene, documentation, harness\n191|\n192|- P3-a Sanitizer scope is undefined by the pinned text and the implemented\n193|  scope is narrower than the comments imply: U+0085 (C1 control), U+2028,\n194|  U+200B, `URN:AX:…` (case), schemeless `user:secret@host/path` are all\n195|  ADMITTED (probe P3). State the exact sanitizer bound in TRACEABILITY.md or\n196|  harden (`unicode.IsControl`, case-fold the AX marker).\n197|- P3-b Content-block members (`type/content/blob_descriptor_id/media_type/\n198|  extensions`) are a producer design not in the pinned text; a block with\n199|  neither content nor descriptor, and one with both, are admitted (P7/P7b).\n200|  State it as a bound or enforce \"typed inline content XOR Blob Descriptor\n201|  reference\".\n202|- P3-c `BuildCaptureManifest` seals a manifest whose items ≠ plan candidates\n203|  with `raw_complete=false` (P5) instead of refusing; §13.14.1 says items are\n204|  \"one per plan candidate\" and §7.8 capture requires \"exact plan-key\n205|  reconciliation\". Refuse at Build, or state why an incomplete-reconciliation\n206|  manifest is a valid archive object.\n207|- P3-d `N-exclusion-config` is an arm-delete (`&& false`), not a narrowing;\n208|  the arm is genuinely pinned (my `R-exclusion-config-narrow`, admitting\n209|  exactly `settings.bak.3`, is KILLED) — replace the row so the harness says\n210|  what it measures.\n211|- P3-e The shipped harness discards per-plant output; `mutants.log` carries\n212|  verdict lines only, while the COMMON CONTRACT asks for per-plant raw logs\n213|  and subprocess exits. Write one log per plant.\n214|- P3-f LOGBOOK OWNERSHIP line still says \"reuses\n215|  `Canonicalize`/`VerifyObjectIdentity` (blobs)\" and in the same sentence\n216|  \"never the attesting `VerifyObjectIdentity` entry\"; results.md claims the\n217|  stale mention was corrected. Production calls neither\n218|  `VerifyObjectIdentity` (only the test fixture does) — fix the sentence.\n219|- P3-g `BoundaryInput.Core` is a caller-asserted boolean; \"only core may\n220|  construct\" is therefore nominal at this entry and the real protection is\n221|  `RefuseUnstableForTarget`. State that bound explicitly.\n222|- P3-h Dead code: `_ = extensionBytes`, `_ = manifest`, `_ = workspace`,\n223|  `kindOf`; the `decode.go:111` comment states the wrong unit (see P2-a).\n224|\n225|## What is clean (verified, not read)\n226|\n227|1. **Spec fidelity, member level** — all 16 closed shapes' member sets and\n228|   all 6 vocabularies extracted from the code equal the pinned text\n229|   member-for-member (raw manifest 11, entry 5, capture manifest 17, item 7,\n230|   basis 6/3, boundary 3/8, proof 9, session 14, actor 7, event 14, evidence\n231|   9, raw reference 4, NativeIdentity 6, WorkspaceBinding 8; 26 kinds, 9\n232|   classes, 5 raw classes, 8 block types, 4 proof kinds, 3 identity kinds;\n233|   visibility/status/actor-kind/disposition/basis/boundary/reason_code\n234|   inline vocabularies). Every array/string bound matches the text (unit\n235|   aside, P2-a). No member the text forbids is admitted; no vocabulary entry\n236|   is missing.\n237|2. **Row-21 exclusion** — `refuseExcludedMember` is called on every native\n238|   item key at all four construction/decode paths (`buildRawEntries`,\n239|   `decodeRawEntries`, `buildCaptureItem`, `decodeCaptureItem`); no other\n240|   entry admits a member key. Every handoff class plus `..` escapes has a\n241|   constructor negative in both manifests; absolute paths are refused\n242|   earlier by the sanitizer (tested). True narrowings of both arms\n243|   (`R-exclusion-config-narrow`, `R-exclusion-replication-narrow`) KILLED 2/2.\n244|   The landed matchers admit `host-channel\\trust.json` and\n245|   `HOST-CHANNEL/trust.json` on POSIX (probe P3x) — hosttrust's contract,\n246|   outside this leaf.\n247|3. **provhost bound** — `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`\n248|   PASS on the candidate tree (225 production files, 5 session-leaf sites,\n249|   0 elsewhere; `logs/provhost-census.log`); module-wide grep: non-test\n250|   `VerifyObjectIdentity` callers only in `internal/sessrepo` (5 sites);\n251|   clonebundle production calls `CalculateObjectIdentity` only. An\n252|   any-claim plant at the agreement site (`R-agreement-site-any-claim`) is\n253|   KILLED 2/2 by the resealed-descriptor negative; `N-descriptor-claim`\n254|   reproduces KILLED 3/3 (see P2-c for the install site).\n255|4. **Blob install** — `InstallRawBlob` delegates to `localstore.PutBlob`\n256|   (stage → fsync → size/digest verify → no-replace install → dir fsync);\n257|   short and long byte streams are refused (P14/P14b), tampered bytes refused\n258|   (`TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent`), double install agrees. The durability\n259|   bound (no write path in this package; crash/idempotency owned by the\n260|   landed localstore fault suites) is stated and accurate.\n261|5. **Producer mutants** — 17 KILLED + control SURVIVED reproduce in the\n262|   isolated copy, 3/3 each, no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` written\n263|   (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; candidate tree diff-clean against the live\n264|   worktree after every run). My four brief-named classes: raw_complete\n265|   ignoring one unknown item KILLED; always-excluded set missing\n266|   `machine_auth` KILLED; raw subset admitting `machine_auth` KILLED;\n267|   capture-item equal-key duplicate at Build KILLED (at Decode SURVIVED —\n268|   P2-b); sanitizer admitting U+001F KILLED.\n269|6. **Race gate** — see next section.\n270|7. **Hygiene** — `gofmt -l` empty, `go vet` clean, `go build ./...` OK,\n271|   `go test ./internal/clonebundle ./internal/provhost ./internal/localstore\n272|   ./internal/canonicaljson -count=1` all ok, `tracecheck` exit 0,\n273|   `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit\n274|   0 on the exact tree; `internal/traceability` untouched; changed paths are\n275|   exactly the 21 candidate paths; README section has test commands and no\n276|   capability/CLI claim; LOGBOOK entry newest-first; sibling bounds stated\n277|   in doc.go, TRACEABILITY.md, results.md.\n278|\n279|## Race gate (item 7)\n280|\n281|The package is untouched by this change: no file outside\n282|`internal/clonebundle`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` changed; nothing imports\n283|`clonebundle`; `go list -deps`/`-test -deps ./internal/sessquery` do not\n284|include it, so the sessquery race binary is byte-for-byte the trunk binary.\n285|The rev2 Change Request validation ran the current 27-command suite (trunk\n286|`888ae3d`, `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m`) and reports\n287|`required=27 green=27 failed=0 missing=0` — the gate is green under the\n288|suite the candidate is measured by; the producer's red figure was the old\n289|600 s default on the pre-PR51 suite, and disclosing it as a host artifact\n290|rather than claiming a pass was the right disposition.\n291|\n292|My own measurement (`logs/sessquery-race.log`): `go test ./internal/sessquery\n293|-race -count=1 -timeout 25m` on the candidate copy → `ok … 390.559s`, wall\n294|394 s, exit 0, zero `DATA RACE` lines; host load averages 14.45 → 9.83 over\n295|the run, with another session's `sessquery.test -test.timeout=25m0s` at\n296|100% CPU at my start and a second sessquery binary appearing mid-run (this\n297|is a shared host; \"while nothing else runs\" was not available). That is\n298|under the old 600 s default even under that contention; the producer's\n299|630 s was measured at load 19–40. Disposition: host-capacity artifact,\n300|not a candidate defect; the 25 m timeout landed on trunk (`888ae3d`,\n301|TASK-260917-3f8mkd) is the right orchestration fix and the rev2 validation\n302|already ran under it. I did not locate the 96 s idle figure on the board\n303|within the review budget and do not claim it.\n304|\n305|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n306|\n307|1. Link descriptor identity to the entry (P1-a): compare the calculated\n308|   descriptor identity with `blob_descriptor_id` at `buildRawEntries` and\n309|   `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors`; negatives + narrowing mutant.\n310|2. Enforce the AX number model (and nested duplicate refusal) on extension\n311|   values at Build and Decode (P1-b); negatives (`1.5`, `2^53`, `2^60`) +\n312|   narrowing mutant.\n313|3. Adopt the environ gates (P2-f) — which fixes the string measure (P2-a);\n314|   one multibyte boundary row.\n315|4. Add Decode-side negatives so every row in the P2-b table is KILLED, plus\n316|   `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` and `InstallRawBlob` negatives (P2-c);\n317|   extend the harness with those rows and per-plant raw logs (P3-e); replace\n318|   `N-exclusion-config` with a narrowing (P3-d); fix the `N-descriptor-claim`\n319|   note or split it per site.\n320|5. Refuse duplicate raw keys in reconciliation (P2-d); re-decode in\n321|   `IdentityDigest` (P2-e).\n322|6. State or enforce the P3-a/b/c/g bounds; fix the LOGBOOK sentence (P3-f)\n323|   and the dead code (P3-h).\n324|\n325|Checklist state left by this review: the four reviewer rows (Implementation\n326|matches AC; Solution fits project architecture; Tests green; Gate … attacked,\n327|not read) are left unchecked; \"If review does not accept the work — verdict\n328|evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\" is\n329|checked. Status routed to `to-dev`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
