{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5e7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0cc-369a-7993-946b-ef774181fd54"},"sequence":334,"recorded_at":1780531400000663,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0cc-ef1f-7b43-a493-b41ad0c94bb2"},"task_id":"01a0b0cc-ef1f-7b43-a493-b41ad0c94bb2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0cc-ef1f-7b43-a493-b41ad0c94bb2","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-12-1\",\n  \"command\": \"R=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-24z2b3; cat $R/TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md; echo \\\"=====MATRIX=====\\\"; cat $R/TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read results and conformance matrix\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# TASK-260830-24z2b3 Results — implement-clone-bundle-and-canonical-session-types\\n\\nStatus: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\\nworktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q`); no commit on the\\nStory branch. This is attempt 2 (run RUN-260917-959ae5): rev1 CR\\nvalidation failed at command 5/27 (`go test ./... -race -count=1`,\\n`internal/sessquery` 600s default-timeout). The candidate below is\\nunchanged from rev1 except one LOGBOOK wording fix; the failure is\\nproven pre-existing and environmental (see \\\"rev1 failure\\\" section).\\n\\n## Delivered\\n\\n`internal/clonebundle` (new package, 11 production files) implements\\nthe Section 13.14.1 clone capture contracts over the landed owners:\\n\\n- Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 (`rawmanifest.go`): closed\\n  envelope, omit-self ID, sorted unique entries, total_bytes sum,\\n  raw class subset, descriptor agreement at construction.\\n- Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (`capturebuild.go`, `captureitem.go`,\\n  `boundary.go`): Source Basis union, Capture Boundary union with\\n  stable-proof coupling, sorted Capture Items, exact excluded\\n  classes, core-derived `raw_complete`, maximal_safe and G2 gates.\\n- Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors (`session.go`): one main actor,\\n  ordered unique event IDs, head subset.\\n- Canonical Event 1.0.0 (`event.go`): 26-kind vocabulary,\\n  visibility, kind-selected payload with content-block rules,\\n  SourceEvidence with synthesized coupling, sorted unique raw refs,\\n  ordinal contiguity.\\n- Identities (`identity.go`): NativeIdentity, WorkspaceBinding,\\n  shared native-key sanitizer (no absolute path, UUIDv7/AX\\n  confusion, embedded credentials, AX markers, control chars).\\n- Immutable generations (`generation.go`): opaque tokens with exact\\n  equality, digest-equality comparison.\\n- Raw evidence descriptors (`blobref.go`): Blob Descriptor shape +\\n  identity via `canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity` with a local\\n  claim comparison (never the attesting entry, per the provhost\\n  no-attestation bound), blob/size agreement, install through\\n  `localstore.PutBlob`.\\n\\nAlso: `TRACEABILITY.md` (clause map), `testdata/mutant_harness.py`\\n(17 narrowing + 1 control), README package section (test commands,\\nno capability claim), LOGBOOK entry (newest-first).\\n\\n## AC coverage: 18 of 18 rows driven\\n\\nSee `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md`: every row names its\\nproduction call site and driving test. No prose-only claims.\\n\\n## Validation reran in attempt 2 (this run, final tree)\\n\\n- `gofmt` check / `go build ./...` / `go vet ./...`: PASS\\n  (log `static-gates.log`)\\n- `go test ./internal/clonebundle/ -count=1`: PASS\\n  (log `pkg-test.log`)\\n- `go test ./internal/clonebundle/ -race -count=1`: PASS\\n  (log `pkg-race.log`)\\n- `go test ./internal/clonebundle/ -cover -count=1`: PASS, 82.2%\\n  statements (log `pkg-cover.log`)\\n- Mutant harness: 17 KILLED + 1 SURVIVED control, exit 0,\\n  `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__` (log `mutants.log`)\\n- Fuzz smoke 14/14 targets: PASS (log `static-gates.log`)\\n- `tracecheck`: PASS; `cataloggen -adopted -check`: PASS\\n  (log `static-gates.log`)\\n- `GOOS=linux` / `GOOS=windows` builds: PASS (log `static-gates.log`)\\n- JSON validation, `task-board validate` (exit 0),\\n  `git diff --check`: PASS (log `static-gates.log`)\\n- `go test ./internal/sessquery -count=1` (no race): PASS\\n  (log `sessquery-norace.log`)\\n\\nAccepted from rev1 attached evidence (not rerun: full-suite runs\\nexceed the single-call bound and the tree is unchanged since rev1\\nexcept the LOGBOOK wording fix): `go test ./... -count=1` PASS\\n38/38, `go test ./... -cover` PASS, rev1 race log showing\\n`internal/clonebundle ok` plus the `sessquery` timeout. The CR\\nvalidation reruns the full suite automatically.\\n\\n## rev1 failure: `sessquery` -race 600s timeout is pre-existing\\n\\n`internal/sessquery` needs ~630s under `-race` on this host (rev1\\nmeasured 630s with `-timeout 25m`, no DATA RACE, no failing\\nassertion) against the 600s default `go test` timeout. Attempt-2\\nproof that the candidate does not cause it:\\n\\n- Same-shard race comparison, back to back:\\n  `go test ./internal/sessquery -race -count=1 -run\\n  TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority` → worktree (candidate\\n  present) 65.6s PASS, clean trunk archive at the same commit\\n  (no candidate) 66.8s PASS (logs `shard-worktree.log`,\\n  `shard-trunk.log`). Identical within host noise.\\n- No package outside `internal/clonebundle` imports it\\n  (`NO_EXTERNAL_IMPORTERS`, see `static-gates.log`), so no other\\n  package's test binary changes.\\n- Full `sessquery` without race PASSES (log\\n  `sessquery-norace.log`); host load averaged 19–40 during these\\n  runs (log `host-load.txt`, shared machine).\\n- `sessquery` is outside this task's story boundary; no\\n  `sessquery` file was touched. The default-timeout race gate\\n  stays red on `sessquery` on this machine by host slowness,\\n  reported as a finding, not fixed by weakening another story's\\n  tests.\\n\\n## Notable finding (rev1, retained)\\n\\nThe first full-suite run reddened\\n`provhost.TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`: that\\ncensus forbids any non-test call to\\n`canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity` outside `internal/sessrepo`.\\nFixed at the root cause following the landed `sessprofile` precedent:\\n`blobref.go` now uses `CalculateObjectIdentity` (shape + digest)\\nwith a local claim comparison and never calls the attesting entry.\\nA wrong-claim negative plus narrowing mutant `N-descriptor-claim`\\npin the new gate. No test was weakened; `provhost` and the full\\nsuite are green. (Attempt 2 additionally corrected the LOGBOOK\\nentry's stale `VerifyObjectIdentity` mention to match the shipped\\ngate; the only tree change since rev1.)\\n\\n## Bounds for siblings (not waived)\\n\\n- Per-kind event payload fact registries past the envelope\\n  (`checkPayload`); maximal_safe planning past the refusal gate;\\n  G2 admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`; Section 7.8\\n  operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`); `internal/traceability`\\n  bindings + re-pin (FINAL leaf).\\n\\n## Base refresh\\n\\nBefore handoff, `origin/main` advanced 7efe385 → 888ae3d\\n(`TASK-260917-3f8mkd: give the race gate an explicit 25m timeout`,\\nconfig-only). Ran `task-board worktree refresh-candidate`, restored\\n`task-board.config.json` to HEAD per the candidate audit rule, and\\nre-verified `go build ./...` + the package suite on the new base\\n(PASS). The refresh resolves the rev1 failure mode at the suite\\nlevel; all attempt-2 logs above were captured on 7efe385 and are\\nunaffected (no production file differs between the bases).\\n\\n## Attachments\\n\\n- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md` (unchanged from rev1)\\n- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (attempt-2 logs:\\n  package suite, mutants, static gates, sessquery shard pair,\\n  sessquery non-race, host load, file manifest)\\n=====MATRIX=====\\n# TASK-260830-24z2b3 Conformance Matrix\\n\\nAuthority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1.\\nPackage: `internal/clonebundle`. Normative spec text is quoted from the\\npinned file; the prose here maps, never restates.\\n\\n## AC coverage: 18 of 18 rows driven\\n\\nEvery row is driven through the named production entry point by the\\nnamed committed test. Prose ratio: **18 of 18 AC rows driven**.\\n\\n| # | AC row | Production call site | Named test |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Raw Object Manifest closed envelope + omit-self ID | `BuildRawObjectManifest`, `DecodeRawObjectManifest` | `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestRawManifestRefusals/decode` |\\n| 2 | RawObjectEntry class subset (credential/auth/runtime/lock forbidden) | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries`, `validRawEntryClass` | `TestRawManifestRefusals/build` (unknown + 4 forbidden-class rows) |\\n| 3 | Sorted unique entries, total_bytes = sum | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries` | `TestRawManifestRefusals` (unsorted, duplicate, total mismatch) |\\n| 4 | Sanitized native keys, never an AX Session ID | `SanitizeNativeKey` | `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer` + key rows in raw/capture/session/event tables |\\n| 5 | Row-21 exclusion allowlist at construction | `refuseExcludedMember` | `TestRawManifestExcludesTrustMaterial`, `TestCaptureManifestExcludesTrustMaterial` |\\n| 6 | Capture Manifest envelope + omit-self ID | `BuildCaptureManifest`, `DecodeCaptureManifest` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestDerivesRawComplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/decode` |\\n| 7 | CaptureItem 9-class vocabulary + included/excluded content rule | `ValidCaptureClass`, `checkItemDisposition` | `TestCaptureClassVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestCaptureItemRefusals` |\\n| 8 | Always-excluded classes never included | `alwaysExcludedClass` | `TestCaptureItemRefusals` (credential, machine_auth, runtime_state, transient_lock rows) |\\n| 9 | excluded_classes exactly the excluded-row classes | `excludedRowClasses`, `excludedClassesExact` | `TestExcludedClassesExactGate`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/decode` (extra, missing, unsorted, unknown) |\\n| 10 | Core-derived raw_complete + plan/object reconciliation | `deriveRawComplete`, `VerifyCaptureReconciliation` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestDerivesRawComplete`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\\n| 11 | Unknown blocks maximal_safe | `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\\n| 12 | Capture Source Basis closed union | `DecodeSourceBasis`, `buildSourceBasis` | `TestSourceBasisRefusals` |\\n| 13 | Capture Boundary union + stable-proof coupling | `DecodeCaptureBoundary`, `buildBoundary`, `checkProofCoupling` | `TestBoundaryRefusals`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\\n| 14 | Unstable is core-created; G2 rejects it | `buildBoundary` (Core), `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestBoundaryRefusals/build_core-only_unstable`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\\n| 15 | NativeIdentity + WorkspaceBinding identities | `DecodeNativeIdentity`, `EncodeNativeIdentity`, `IdentityDigest`, `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` | `TestNativeIdentityRoundTrip`, `TestIdentityDigestIsStable`, `TestIdentityRefusals` |\\n| 16 | Canonical Session + Actor rules (one main, event/head IDs) | `BuildCanonicalSession`, `DecodeCanonicalSession` | `TestBuildCanonicalSessionRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalSessionRefusals` |\\n| 17 | Canonical Event + SourceEvidence + raw refs + ordinals + generations | `BuildCanonicalEvent`, `DecodeCanonicalEvent`, `DecodeSourceEvidence`, `checkPayload`, `CheckOrdinalContiguity`, `ParseGeneration` | `TestEventKindVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals`, `TestOrdinalContiguity`, `TestGenerationRefusals` |\\n| 18 | Blob Descriptor identity + byte-count agreement + no-replace install | `VerifyDescriptorAgreement`, `InstallRawBlob`, `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` | `TestBlobAgreementRefusals`, `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip` |\\n\\n## Negative/refusal evidence\\n\\nEvery refusal above fails when the gate admits what it must reject:\\nthe 17 narrowing mutants in `internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py`\\nweaken each gate to admit exactly one forbidden member and the named\\nkiller fails (17 KILLED, 1 harmless SURVIVED control). Per-plant\\nresults are in the producer evidence tar.\\n\\n## Landed-owner reuse (not new behavior, cited not counted)\\n\\n| Scope | Owner | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Section 7.8 operation frames (capture-plan/capture/normalize fresh isolated sinks; probe/manifest/discover/inspect read-only) | `internal/sessadapter` (`CheckRequestBody`, `CheckSuccessBody`, `CheckFreshSink`) | landed sessadapter suite, green in this run |\\n| Section 10.2 crash/idempotency discipline (fsync, atomic no-replace, quarantine) | `internal/localstore` | landed localstore fault suites, green in this run; delegation proven by `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` |\\n| Closed-shape registry rows for these schemas | `internal/canonicaljson` (`rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape`, census-pinned) | intentionally not replaced; this package is the validating owner (see `doc.go`) |\\n\\n## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\\n\\n- Per-kind Canonical Event payload fact registries beyond the\\n  Section 13.14.1 envelope in `checkPayload` (normalization sibling).\\n- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\\n  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\\n- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\\n- Section 7.8 capture-plan/capture/normalize operation wiring\\n  (stays `sessadapter`-owned).\\n- `internal/traceability` registry bindings and digest re-pin\\n  (Story FINAL leaf).\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 12487,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3122,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
