{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c82f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0cc-369a-7993-946b-ef774181fd54"},"sequence":626,"recorded_at":1780531400001247,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0cd68bb756ba084e51f81342037","text":"Read text file `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Clone Bundle Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-24z2b3)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/clonebundle`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1.\n5|The Story's FINAL leaf carries the `internal/traceability` registry\n6|bindings and re-pin; this file is the first-leaf clause record.\n7|\n8|## Why this package validates instead of canonicaljson\n9|\n10|The `canonicaljson` closed-shape registry keeps\n11|`rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows for\n12|`clone-raw-object-manifest`, `clone-capture-manifest`,\n13|`canonical-session`, and `canonical-event` 1.0.0, and that table's\n14|census pins every row. Replacing them would fork shape ownership, so\n15|this package is the validating owner: it reuses\n16|`canonicaljson.Canonicalize` (byte transform),\n17|`canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity` plus a local claim comparison\n18|(Blob Descriptors; never the attesting entry, per the provhost\n19|no-attestation bound),\n20|`sessadapter.DecodeTuple` (Environment Tuples),\n21|`environ.CheckExtensions` (extension keys),\n22|`scalar` (digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, paths),\n23|`hosttrust` (row-21 exclusion matchers), and\n24|`localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob` (blob install). No rule is\n25|reimplemented where a landed owner exists.\n26|\n27|## Clause map\n28|\n29|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n30||---|---|---|\n31|| 13.14.1 Raw Manifest closed envelope + self ID | `BuildRawObjectManifest`, `DecodeRawObjectManifest` | `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestRawManifestRefusals/decode` |\n32|| 13.14.1 RawObjectEntry class subset (no credential/auth/runtime/lock) | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries` | `TestRawManifestRefusals/build` (5 class rows) |\n33|| 13.14.1 sorted unique entries, total_bytes sum | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries` | `TestRawManifestRefusals` (unsorted, duplicate, total mismatch) |\n34|| 13.14.1 sanitized native key, never an AX Session ID | `SanitizeNativeKey` | `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer`, raw/capture/session/event refusal rows |\n35|| Row 21 exclusion allowlist at construction | `refuseExcludedMember` | `TestRawManifestExcludesTrustMaterial`, `TestCaptureManifestExcludesTrustMaterial` |\n36|| 13.14.1 CaptureItem 9-class vocabulary | `ValidCaptureClass`, `buildCaptureItem`, `decodeCaptureItem` | `TestCaptureClassVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestCaptureItemRefusals` |\n37|| 13.14.1 included/excluded content rule | `checkItemDisposition` | `TestCaptureItemRefusals` (6 content rows) |\n38|| 13.14.1 always-excluded classes never included | `alwaysExcludedClass` | `TestCaptureItemRefusals` (4 class rows) |\n39|| 13.14.1 exact excluded_classes | `excludedRowClasses`, `excludedClassesExact` | `TestExcludedClassesExactGate`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/decode` |\n40|| 13.14.1 core-derived raw_complete + reconciliation | `deriveRawComplete`, `VerifyCaptureReconciliation` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestDerivesRawComplete`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\n41|| 13.14.1 unknown blocks maximal_safe | `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\n42|| 13.14.1 Capture Source Basis union | `DecodeSourceBasis`, `buildSourceBasis` | `TestSourceBasisRefusals` |\n43|| 13.14.1 Capture Boundary union, stable proof coupling | `DecodeCaptureBoundary`, `buildBoundary`, `checkProofCoupling` | `TestBoundaryRefusals`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n44|| 13.14.1 unstable is core-created, G2 rejects | `buildBoundary` (Core), `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestBoundaryRefusals/build_core-only_unstable`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n45|| 13.14.1 NativeIdentity closed shape | `DecodeNativeIdentity`, `EncodeNativeIdentity` | `TestNativeIdentityRoundTrip`, `TestIdentityRefusals/native_identity` |\n46|| 13.14.1 source_identity_digest terminal digest | `IdentityDigest` | `TestIdentityDigestIsStable`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip` |\n47|| 13.14.1 WorkspaceBinding closed shape, normalized cwd | `DecodeWorkspaceBinding`, `checkCwdRelative` | `TestIdentityRefusals/workspace_binding` |\n48|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session + Actor rules | `BuildCanonicalSession`, `DecodeCanonicalSession` | `TestBuildCanonicalSessionRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalSessionRefusals` |\n49|| 13.14.1 Canonical Event envelope + 26 kinds + visibility | `BuildCanonicalEvent`, `DecodeCanonicalEvent`, `ValidEventKind` | `TestEventKindVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals` |\n50|| 13.14.1 SourceEvidence + RawReference + synthesized coupling | `DecodeSourceEvidence`, `buildSourceEvidence`, `checkEvidenceCoupling` | `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/evidence` |\n51|| 13.14.1 message-like content blocks, 64 KiB inline bound | `checkPayload`, `checkContentBlocks` | `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/build_envelope` (block rows + 64 KiB boundary) |\n52|| 13.14.1 contiguous ordinals from zero | `CheckOrdinalContiguity` | `TestOrdinalContiguity` |\n53|| 13.14.1 immutable generations | `ParseGeneration`, `Generation.Equal`, `CheckDigestsEqual` | `TestGenerationRefusals`, `TestBoundaryRefusals` |\n54|| 13.14.1 reverse-DNS extensions, no normative reference | `encodeExtensions`, `checkExtensions` | contract round trips + `bad extensions` rows in every refusal table |\n55|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor identity + byte-count agreement | `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` | `TestBlobAgreementRefusals`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` row |\n56|| 10.2 no-replace install (fsync + verify + atomic) | `InstallRawBlob` via `localstore.PutBlob` | `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` |\n57|| 7.8 tuple/probe/manifest/discover/inspect reuse | `sessadapter.DecodeTuple` at every `source_environment` | `bad tuple` rows in raw/capture/session/event tables |\n58|| Byte-identical construction | all Build entries | `RoundTrip` tests rebuild and compare bytes |\n59|\n60|## Durability bound\n61|\n62|This package performs no durable write: `InstallRawBlob` delegates\n63|every byte to `localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob` (no-replace install,\n64|fsync, size/digest verification, quarantine on collision). The\n65|landed crash/idempotency evidence for that discipline lives with\n66|`internal/localstore` (`object_store_test.go`,\n67|`object_store_fault_unix_test.go`, projection fault suites);\n68|`TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` proves the delegation end to end\n69|(double install agrees, tampered bytes refuse). No second write\n70|path exists in this package.\n71|\n72|## Stated bounds (sibling scope)\n73|\n74|- Per-kind Canonical Event payload fact registries beyond the\n75|  Section 13.14.1 envelope enforced in `checkPayload` (normalization\n76|  sibling).\n77|- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\n78|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\n79|- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\n80|- Section 7.8 capture-plan/capture/normalize operation wiring\n81|  (stays owned by `sessadapter`); this package owns the contracts\n82|  those operations produce, not the operation frames.\n83|- `internal/traceability` registry bindings and digest re-pin\n84|  (Story FINAL leaf).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c831","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0cc-369a-7993-946b-ef774181fd54"},"sequence":627,"recorded_at":1780531400001249,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c76039bf-a435-41d5-be3c-7dbf6b953ab3"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0cd6a697229b901a9971e8f9272","text":"Read text file `internal/clonebundle/fixtures_test.go`.\n1|package clonebundle\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n5|\t\"encoding/hex\"\n6|\t\"encoding/json\"\n7|\t\"fmt\"\n8|\t\"os\"\n9|\t\"path/filepath\"\n10|\t\"runtime\"\n11|\t\"testing\"\n12|\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/localstore\"\n15|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n16|)\n17|\n18|// Shared fixtures for the clonebundle suite. Every literal is\n19|// hand-written and independent of production constants: the verdict\n20|// always comes from production; the vectors never do.\n21|\n22|const (\n23|\tfixtureOperationID = \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ac\"\n24|\tfixtureBundleID    = \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890b1\"\n25|\tfixtureSessionID   = \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890c2\"\n26|\tfixtureRecordSeed  = \"test-session-record\"\n27|\tfixtureHostID      = \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890d3\"\n28|\tfixtureActorMain   = \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890e4\"\n29|\tfixtureActorSub    = \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890f5\"\n30|\tfixtureTurnID      = \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890a6\"\n31|\tfixtureCreatedAt   = \"2026-09-17T04:05:00.000Z\"\n32|\tfixtureWorkspaceID = \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890b7\"\n33|)\n34|\n35|func fixtureDigest(seed string) string {\n36|\tsum := sha256.Sum256([]byte(seed))\n37|\treturn \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(sum[:])\n38|}\n39|\n40|func fixtureTupleJSON() string {\n41|\treturn fmt.Sprintf(`{\"environment_id\":\"test.env\",\"environment_version\":\"2.1.0\",\"platform\":\"linux\",\"architecture\":\"amd64\",\"store_schema_fingerprint\":%q,\"adapter_version\":\"1.2.3\"}`,\n42|\t\tfixtureDigest(\"test-store-fingerprint\"))\n43|}\n44|\n45|func fixtureWorkspaceJSON() string {\n46|\treturn fmt.Sprintf(`{\"logical_workspace_id\":%q,\"cwd_relative\":\"work/trees/alpha\",\"repository_remote_fingerprints\":[%q],\"branch\":\"main\",\"head_digest\":%q,\"index_digest\":null,\"working_tree_digest\":null,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n47|\t\tfixtureWorkspaceID, fixtureDigest(\"test-remote\"), fixtureDigest(\"test-head\"))\n48|}\n49|\n50|func fixtureNativeIdentity() NativeIdentity {\n51|\tworkspace, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(fixtureWorkspaceID)\n52|\tif err != nil {\n53|\t\tpanic(err)\n54|\t}\n55|\treturn NativeIdentity{\n56|\t\tNativeSessionID:    \"native-session-alpha\",\n57|\t\tIdentityKind:       \"provider_native\",\n58|\t\tLogicalWorkspaceID: workspace,\n59|\t}\n60|}\n61|\n62|func mustDigest(t *testing.T, value string) scalar.Digest {\n63|\tt.Helper()\n64|\tdigest, err := scalar.ParseDigest(value)\n65|\tif err != nil {\n66|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ParseDigest(%q) error = %v\", value, err)\n67|\t}\n68|\treturn digest\n69|}\n70|\n71|func strptr(value string) *string { return &value }\n72|\n73|func u64ptr(value uint64) *uint64 { return &value }\n74|\n75|// makeDescriptor builds one valid Section 10.2 Blob Descriptor for\n76|// the given payload through the canonicaljson production entries:\n77|// the shape validates and the identity verifies before the fixture\n78|// is returned.\n79|func makeDescriptor(t *testing.T, payload []byte) (descriptor []byte, blobID, descriptorID string, size uint64) {\n80|\tt.Helper()\n81|\tsum := sha256.Sum256(payload)\n82|\tblobID = \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(sum[:])\n83|\tsize = uint64(len(payload))\n84|\tvar chunks []any\n85|\tif len(payload) > 0 {\n86|\t\tchunks = []any{map[string]any{\n87|\t\t\t\"index\":    0,\n88|\t\t\t\"offset\":   0,\n89|\t\t\t\"size\":     size,\n90|\t\t\t\"chunk_id\": blobID,\n91|\t\t}}\n92|\t} else {\n93|\t\tchunks = []any{}\n94|\t}\n95|\tobject := map[string]any{\n96|\t\t\"schema\":         \"urn:ax:schema:blob\",\n97|\t\t\"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n98|\t\t\"descriptor_id\":  fixtureDigest(\"placeholder-descriptor\"),\n99|\t\t\"blob_id\":        blobID,\n100|\t\t\"size\":           size,\n101|\t\t\"media_type\":     \"application/octet-stream\",\n102|\t\t\"chunks\":         chunks,\n103|\t}\n104|\tplain, err := json.Marshal(object)\n105|\tif err != nil {\n106|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n107|\t}\n108|\tcalculated, _, err := canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity(plain)\n109|\tif err != nil {\n110|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CalculateObjectIdentity(fixture descriptor) error = %v\", err)\n111|\t}\n112|\tobject[\"descriptor_id\"] = calculated.String()\n113|\tdescriptor, err = json.Marshal(object)\n114|\tif err != nil {\n115|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n116|\t}\n117|\tif _, _, err := canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity(descriptor); err != nil {\n118|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"VerifyObjectIdentity(fixture descriptor) error = %v\", err)\n119|\t}\n120|\treturn descriptor, blobID, calculated.String(), size\n121|}\n122|\n123|func openFixtureStore(t *testing.T) *localstore.ObjectStore {\n124|\tt.Helper()\n125|\thome := t.TempDir()\n126|\tconfig := filepath.Join(home, \"config\")\n127|\tif err := os.Mkdir(config, 0o700); err != nil {\n128|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n129|\t}\n130|\tplatform := scalar.PlatformLinux\n131|\tif runtime.GOOS == \"darwin\" {\n132|\t\tplatform = scalar.PlatformMacOS\n133|\t} else if runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" {\n134|\t\tplatform = scalar.PlatformWindows\n135|\t}\n136|\tresolved, err := localstore.ResolvePaths(localstore.ResolveRequest{\n137|\t\tPlatform: platform,\n138|\t\tFlags: map[string]string{\n139|\t\t\t\"--config\":      filepath.Join(config, \"config.toml\"),\n140|\t\t\t\"--data-dir\":    filepath.Join(home, \"data\"),\n141|\t\t\t\"--state-dir\":   filepath.Join(home, \"state\"),\n142|\t\t\t\"--cache-dir\":   filepath.Join(home, \"cache\"),\n143|\t\t\t\"--runtime-dir\": filepath.Join(home, \"runtime\"),\n144|\t\t},\n145|\t\tEnvironment:  map[string]string{},\n146|\t\tHomeDir:      home,\n147|\t\tTemporaryDir: filepath.Join(home, \"temporary\"),\n148|\t})\n149|\tif err != nil {\n150|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ResolvePaths() error = %v\", err)\n151|\t}\n152|\tstore, err := localstore.OpenObjectStore(resolved)\n153|\tif err != nil {\n154|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"OpenObjectStore() error = %v\", err)\n155|\t}\n156|\treturn store\n157|}\n158|\n159|func validEntryInputs(t *testing.T) []EntryInput {\n160|\tt.Helper()\n161|\tfirst, firstBlob, firstDescriptor, firstSize := makeDescriptor(t, []byte(\"first-raw-object\"))\n162|\tsecond, secondBlob, secondDescriptor, secondSize := makeDescriptor(t, []byte(\"second-raw-object\"))\n163|\treturn []EntryInput{\n164|\t\t{NativeItemKey: \"store/blob-a\", Class: \"durable_payload\", ByteCount: firstSize, BlobID: firstBlob, DescriptorID: firstDescriptor, Descriptor: first},\n165|\t\t{NativeItemKey: \"store/blob-b\", Class: \"durable_sidecar\", ByteCount: secondSize, BlobID: secondBlob, DescriptorID: secondDescriptor, Descriptor: second},\n166|\t}\n167|}\n168|\n169|func validCaptureItems(t *testing.T) []CaptureItemInput {\n170|\tt.Helper()\n171|\t_, _, firstDescriptor, firstSize := makeDescriptor(t, []byte(\"first-raw-object\"))\n172|\t_, _, secondDescriptor, secondSize := makeDescriptor(t, []byte(\"second-raw-object\"))\n173|\tfirstCount := firstSize\n174|\tsecondCount := secondSize\n175|\treturn []CaptureItemInput{\n176|\t\t{NativeItemKey: \"store/blob-a\", Class: \"durable_payload\", Disposition: \"included\", BlobDescriptorID: &firstDescriptor, ByteCount: &firstCount},\n177|\t\t{NativeItemKey: \"store/blob-b\", Class: \"durable_sidecar\", Disposition: \"included\", BlobDescriptorID: &secondDescriptor, ByteCount: &secondCount},\n178|\t\t{NativeItemKey: \"store/token-cache\", Class: \"credential\", Disposition: \"excluded\", ExclusionReason: strptr(\"credential_excluded\")},\n179|\t}\n180|}\n181|\n182|func validBoundaryInput() BoundaryInput {\n183|\treturn BoundaryInput{\n184|\t\tKind:              \"stable\",\n185|\t\tProofKind:         \"closed_store\",\n186|\t\tGeneration:        \"generation-42\",\n187|\t\tPreCaptureDigest:  fixtureDigest(\"test-pre-capture\"),\n188|\t\tPostCaptureDigest: fixtureDigest(\"test-pre-capture\"),\n189|\t\tInputBlocked:      true,\n190|\t\tForegroundIdle:    true,\n191|\t\tBackgroundIdle:    true,\n192|\t}\n193|}\n194|\n195|func validCaptureInput(t *testing.T) CaptureManifestInput {\n196|\tt.Helper()\n197|\treturn CaptureManifestInput{\n198|\t\tOperationID: fixtureOperationID,\n199|\t\tBundleID:    fixtureBundleID,\n200|\t\tSourceBasis: SourceBasisInput{\n201|\t\t\tKind:                     \"ax_session\",\n202|\t\t\tSourceSessionID:          fixtureSessionID,\n203|\t\t\tSourceSessionRecordID:    fixtureDigest(fixtureRecordSeed),\n204|\t\t\tSourceCheckpointID:       fixtureDigest(\"test-checkpoint\"),\n205|\t\t\tSourceProviderIdentityID: fixtureDigest(\"test-provider-identity\"),\n206|\t\t},\n207|\t\tSourceEnvironment:   []byte(fixtureTupleJSON()),\n208|\t\tSourceIdentity:      fixtureNativeIdentity(),\n209|\t\tCapturePlanDigest:   fixtureDigest(\"test-capture-plan\"),\n210|\t\tBoundary:            validBoundaryInput(),\n211|\t\tSourceRawManifestID: fixtureDigest(\"test-raw-manifest\"),\n212|\t\tItems:               validCaptureItems(t),\n213|\t\tPlanKeys:            []string{\"store/blob-a\", \"store/blob-b\", \"store/token-cache\"},\n214|\t\tRawKeys:             []string{\"store/blob-a\", \"store/blob-b\"},\n215|\t\tCreatedByHostID:     fixtureHostID,\n216|\t\tCreatedAt:           fixtureCreatedAt,\n217|\t}\n218|}\n219|\n220|func validSessionInput() CanonicalSessionInput {\n221|\treturn CanonicalSessionInput{\n222|\t\tLogicalSessionID:      fixtureSessionID,\n223|\t\tSourceEnvironment:     []byte(fixtureTupleJSON()),\n224|\t\tSourceNativeSessionID: \"native-session-alpha\",\n225|\t\tTitle:                 strptr(\"alpha session\"),\n226|\t\tWorkspace:             []byte(fixtureWorkspaceJSON()),\n227|\t\tActors: []ActorInput{\n228|\t\t\t{ActorID: fixtureActorMain, Kind: \"main\", Name: strptr(\"main\")},\n229|\t\t\t{ActorID: fixtureActorSub, Kind: \"subagent\", ParentActorID: strptr(fixtureActorMain)},\n230|\t\t},\n231|\t\tEventIDs:     []string{fixtureDigest(\"test-event-0\"), fixtureDigest(\"test-event-1\")},\n232|\t\tHeadEventIDs: []string{fixtureDigest(\"test-event-1\")},\n233|\t\tCreatedAt:    strptr(fixtureCreatedAt),\n234|\t}\n235|}\n236|\n237|func validEventInput(status string) CanonicalEventInput {\n238|\tinput := CanonicalEventInput{\n239|\t\tLogicalSessionID: fixtureSessionID,\n240|\t\tOrdinal:          0,\n241|\t\tActorID:          fixtureActorMain,\n242|\t\tKind:             \"user_message\",\n243|\t\tVisibility:       \"public\",\n244|\t\tPayload:          []byte(`{\"content_blocks\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"content\":\"hello\"}],\"extensions\":{}}`),\n245|\t\tEvidence: EvidenceInput{\n246|\t\t\tEnvironment:     []byte(fixtureTupleJSON()),\n247|\t\t\tNativeSessionID: \"native-session-alpha\",\n248|\t\t\tNativeEventID:   strptr(\"native-event-1\"),\n249|\t\t\tNativeType:      strptr(\"chat.message\"),\n250|\t\t\tRawRefs: []RawRefInput{\n251|\t\t\t\t{ManifestID: fixtureDigest(\"test-raw-manifest\"), BlobDescriptorID: fixtureDigest(\"test-descriptor\"), Offset: 0, Length: 128},\n252|\t\t\t},\n253|\t\t\tCaptureStatus: status,\n254|\t\t\tReasonCodes:   []string{\"source_complete\"},\n255|\t\t},\n256|\t}\n257|\tif status == \"synthesized\" {\n258|\t\tinput.Evidence.NativeEventID = nil\n259|\t\tinput.Evidence.CoreOperationID = strptr(fixtureOperationID)\n260|\t}\n261|\treturn input\n262|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
